Some parts of this repository belong to others and keep their own terms.
Nothing above changes those terms.

- Map data (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, under the Open Database
  License (ODbL) 1.0: roads, water, places, land use and glaciers. Data
  files in public/data that are built from OpenStreetMap or Microsoft
  data are made available under the ODbL 1.0.
- Elevation behind the terrain in public/data/state from AWS Terrain
  Tiles (Tilezen Joerd, on the Registry of Open Data on AWS): 3DEP
  (formerly NED), GMTED2010 and SRTM terrain data courtesy of the U.S.
  Geological Survey, in the public domain.
- Building outlines from Microsoft US Building Footprints, under the
  ODbL 1.0.
- Storm drain, road and stream data from the City of Bonney Lake and
  Pierce County GIS, used under each provider's terms and provided as
  is, without warranty.
- Storm drain data from the City of Federal Way GIS, provided as is,
  without warranty of any kind. The City of Federal Way prohibits
  commercial use or sale of its data without written authorization.
- Storm drain data from the City of Sammamish GIS, used under the city's
  terms: provided as is, without warranty or any representation of
  accuracy, timeliness or completeness.
- Storm drain data from the City of Mercer Island, City of Maple Valley
  and City of Covington GIS, used under each provider's terms and
  provided as is, without warranty. The City of Mercer Island makes no
  representation or warranty about the accuracy or currency of its GIS
  data.
- Storm drain data from the City of SeaTac GIS, for informational
  purposes only and provided as is, as available and with all faults,
  without warranty of any kind.
- Storm drain data from the City of Burien GIS, under CC BY-NC
  (attribution, non-commercial), provided as is, without warranty or
  any representation of accuracy, timeliness or completeness.
- Storm drain data from the City of Tukwila GIS (a May 2020 snapshot of
  the city's public utility viewer), provided as is, without warranty.
- Storm drain data from the City of Des Moines and City of Normandy Park
  GIS, used under each provider's terms and provided as is, without
  warranty.
- Storm drain data from the City of Shoreline, City of Lake Forest Park
  and City of Kenmore GIS, used under each provider's terms and provided
  as is, without warranty of any kind. The City of Shoreline notes that
  its data is not official.
- Storm drain data from the City of Bothell, City of Woodinville and City
  of Duvall GIS, used under each provider's terms and provided as is,
  without warranty. The City of Woodinville does not warrant the
  accuracy, currency, completeness or quality of its data, and use is at
  the user's sole risk. The City of Duvall disclaims any warranty of
  merchantability or fitness for any particular purpose and makes no
  representation about the accuracy, currency, completeness or quality
  of its data.
- Storm drain data from the City of Redmond, under the Redmond Data Terms
  of Use: The data made available here has been modified for use from
  its original source, which is the City of Redmond. The City of Redmond
  makes no claims as to the completeness, timeliness, accuracy or
  content of any data contained in this application; makes any
  representation of any kind, including, but not limited to, warranty of
  the accuracy or fitness for a particular use; nor are any such
  warranties to be implied or inferred with respect to the information
  or data furnished herein. The data is subject to change as
  modifications and updates are complete. It is understood that the
  information contained in the web feed is being used at one's own risk.
- Storm drain data from the City of Newcastle (a 2020 snapshot), City of
  Clyde Hill, City of Medina and City of North Bend GIS, from the cities'
  public map services. None states license terms; the data is used as
  published and provided as is, without warranty of any kind. Medina
  data (c) City of Medina.
- Storm drain data: City of Kent GIS, from a public map service hosted
  by Woolpert (not an official open-data release), provided as is,
  without warranty of any kind. The service states no license terms.
- Salmon and steelhead distribution data (coho statewide, in Pierce
  County and in public/data/salmon) from SWIFD, the Statewide Washington
  Integrated Fish Distribution of the Washington Department of Fish and
  Wildlife and the Northwest Indian Fisheries Commission, used under
  WDFW's terms and provided as is, without warranty.
- Stream and lake data from the USGS National Hydrography Dataset, place
  outlines from the US Census Bureau, and Natural Earth data, all in the
